  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion lag: The model consistently fails to anticipate the sharp price drop from ~79 to ~67 occurring 5-10 days after the forecast date, often predicting a flat or slightly rising trend instead. Apply a negative bias adjustment of 5-8 EUR for the 5-15 day horizon when history shows a recent peak above 78 followed by a downward inflection.",
    "Adjust for delayed recovery overshoot: The model underestimates the magnitude and speed of the rebound (from ~67 back to ~80) occurring 15-25 days out. When sentiment history shows a spike (e.g., 0.33) coinciding with the trough, increase the forecast slope by 1.5x to capture the rapid recovery to 80+.",
    "Ignore low-magnitude sentiment signals: Sentiment values of 0.20-0.25 do not correlate with immediate price movements in this dataset; rely primarily on price momentum and structural mean reversion rather than these weak sentiment inputs.",
    "Apply horizon-specific volatility scaling: The model's 30-day forecast is too smooth (low volatility). Increase the variance of the forecast path to reflect the observed swing of 13 EUR between the trough and peak, rather than the model's predicted 1-2 EUR drift."
  ]
}
